        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Colorless</strong>​ is a narrative exploration game centered on the theme of &quot;Bugs.&quot; Players enter a seaside town where everything is uniformly tinted with an orderly green. However, dissonant &quot;Fragments of Color&quot; begin to appear like system glitches, shattering the eternal calm.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >◆ <strong>A Unique Narrative Told Through Color</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Why is the world only green? What do the sudden colorful &quot;Bugs&quot; signify? By interacting with the environment, completing tasks for the residents, and collecting scattered puzzle pieces, you will gradually uncover the shocking truth of this world. Every choice to &quot;restore&quot; an object (by painting it green) or to &quot;color&quot; it (by imparting hue) shapes your understanding of order and freedom.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >◆ <strong>Philosophical Puzzles</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The puzzles are seamlessly woven into the environment and story. Whether it's repairing a sign or fulfilling a specific order, each task is designed to provoke deep reflection on the world's operating principles. Collecting all the puzzle pieces to complete the final picture is the key to unraveling all mysteries.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >◆ <strong>Retro-Future Visual Aesthetic</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game's art style employs a retro aesthetic, using high-contrast color blocks and pixel art to construct a unique world that feels both nostalgic and futuristic.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Colorless</strong>​ is a narrative exploration game centered on the theme of &quot;Bugs.&quot; Players enter a seaside town where everything is uniformly tinted with an orderly green. However, dissonant &quot;Fragments of Color&quot; begin to appear like system glitches, shattering the eternal calm.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >◆ <strong>A Unique Narrative Told Through Color</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Why is the world only green? What do the sudden colorful &quot;Bugs&quot; signify? By interacting with the environment, completing tasks for the residents, and collecting scattered puzzle pieces, you will gradually uncover the shocking truth of this world. Every choice to &quot;restore&quot; an object (by painting it green) or to &quot;color&quot; it (by imparting hue) shapes your understanding of order and freedom.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >◆ <strong>Philosophical Puzzles</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The puzzles are seamlessly woven into the environment and story. Whether it's repairing a sign or fulfilling a specific order, each task is designed to provoke deep reflection on the world's operating principles. Collecting all the puzzle pieces to complete the final picture is the key to unraveling all mysteries.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >◆ <strong>Retro-Future Visual Aesthetic</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game's art style employs a retro aesthetic, using high-contrast color blocks and pixel art to construct a unique world that feels both nostalgic and futuristic.</p>",
        "short_description": "In a world ruled by a single shade of green, color is the ultimate taboo—and the ultimate truth. Explore, restore, and then choose: Will you maintain the illusion of order, or embrace the chaos of color?",
